#show: nsf-doc.with(page-limit: 1, draft: DRAFT, title: [Synergistic Activities — Aaron Cherian])

+ *Open-source research tooling for data quality and benchmarking.*
  Designs and builds diagnostics and benchmarking tools for the FreeMoCap
  platform, giving the research community practical instruments for
  assessing the quality and reliability of markerless motion-capture data
  across systems and software versions.

+ *Validation research and publication.* Conducts validation studies of
  open-source markerless motion capture against established marker-based
  standards and publishes the results in the research literature, providing
  the community with openly available evidence about the capabilities and
  limitations of accessible motion-capture methods.

+ *Collaborative research across application domains.* Co-authors research
  papers with external researchers applying motion capture in their own
  domains, supporting the adoption of accessible movement measurement in
  fields far from the original development team's expertise and transferring
  methods knowledge to new research communities.

+ *Interface regularization and contributor onboarding.* Works to regularize
  and document the project's application programming interfaces and
  validation strategies, explicitly to lower the technical barriers for
  outside developers and researchers to contribute to the ecosystem —
  transferring architectural knowledge beyond the core development team.

+ *Community teaching and mentoring.* Teaches and mentors students,
  early-career researchers, and professionals through the FreeMoCap
  community channels, providing guidance on motion-capture methodology,
  data quality, and open research practice.
